.TH GPT 1
.SH NAME
gpt \- compiler, interpreter and translator for the G-Portugol programming language

.SH SYNOPSIS
  gpt
[
.BR \-vhid
] [
.BI \-ots
output_file
] [
.BI \-a
arch
] file1 file2 ...

.SH DESCRIPTION
.I gpt
is a simple compiler for the G-Porutol Language. It is possible to have
a list of files to be included in the compilation setting the GPT_INCLUDE
environment variable, wich should have a list of file paths separated with ":".
.I gpt
refuses to write an output file over one of the input files, whatever path
or link leads to it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-v
Shows version information and exits.
.br
.ns
.TP
.BI \-h
Shows a summary of options and exits.
.br
.ns
.TP
.TP
.BI \-i
Execute
.I interpreting
the source code.
.br
.ns
.TP
.BI \-d
Shows tips in the error report.
.br
.ns
.TP
.BI \-o " output_file"
Compile the source code and save the resulting binary with the name
.I output_file.
Without this option the binary is named after the first source file without
its extension, in the current directory; a source file with no extension
gives a binary with the
.I .out
extension
.RI ( .exe
on Windows).
On Windows, a source file with the
.I .exe
extension gives a binary whose name ends in
.I .out.exe ,
so the source is not replaced.
The generated code is x86-64 (an ELF64 executable on GNU/Linux, a PE32+
executable on Windows) or arm64 (an ELF64 executable on GNU/Linux), as chosen
with
.BR \-a ;
on a machine that is neither, use
.B \-t
and compile the C code with the system compiler.
For x86-64,
.BR nasm (1)
builds the executable.
For arm64,
.BR as (1)
and
.BR ld (1)
from binutils build the executable; on a machine that is not arm64 they are
the cross tools
.B aarch64-linux-gnu-as
and
.BR aarch64-linux-gnu-ld .
On Windows and GNU/Linux these tools are looked up first in the directory of
.I gpt
and then in the directories of
.BR PATH ;
the current directory is used only when
.B PATH
names it.
.br
.ns
.TP
.BI \-t " output_file"
Translates the source code to the C programming language and saves the
resulting file as
.I output_file.
.br
.ns
.TP
.BI \-s " output_file"
Compiles the source code to assembly source. Saves the resulting code as
.I output_file.
.br
.ns
.TP
.BI \-a " arch"
Selects the architecture of the code written by
.B \-o
and
.BR \-s :
.B x86-64
(NASM syntax) or
.B arm64
(GNU assembler syntax for AArch64).
The default is the architecture of the machine running
.IR gpt ;
a 32-bit x86
.I gpt
on GNU/Linux uses
.B x86-64
when the kernel is 64-bit.
.br
.ns
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nasm (1),
.BR as (1),
.BR ld (1)

.SH ADDITIONAL INFORMATION

For further information, visit the website:
.br
.BI https://gportugol.github.io

